Thank you to Grunt for making a variant of Nethack with some cool
patches & stuff.  That said, I have a list of bugs I found:

. you get messages like "you hit it" as if you can't see the monster
when you can.
. iron shoes are called iron iron shoes.  sounds kinda silly..
. sacrificing seems to be broken.  In two different games, the first
time I sacrifice (alter is already co-aligned), it says, "an object
appears at your feet.." but nothing is there except the corpse of the
monster I just sacrificed.  and then you can sacrifice the same corpse
again, this time it burns up and lowers the prayer timeout because it
acts like I just got a gift.
. I found a werejackel on L1 and EXPL1, and werefoo seem a lot more
common in general.  I don't think this is intended.
. finally, my game crashed when I killed a giant mummy over an alter on
Lvl 4 (no poly trap on the level).  The game was recovered but I later
died because recover didn't seem to work right: I found out what "a
trickery" means when on the scoreboard as the cause of death.
. the tile mode doens't seem to work.  I don't mind playing without
tiles, but I like tiles better.  Could it be because the three new
monsters don't have tiles for them?

Other comments:
.  I think it would be better if dead dwarvish watchman and dwarvish
werejackels, should be called 'dwarvish watchman corpse' or 'dwarvish
werejackel corpse' instead of just 'dwarf corpse,' (same with other
races and werefoo, etc) but maybe you think it's better the way it is,
that's cool.  a question: When it's called 'dwarf corpse' when it's the
corpse of a dwarvish watchman, does it still count as the level of a
watchman when sacrificing or the level of a dwarf?
.  I REALLY don't like fumbling when I have 9 dexterity.  fumbling with
low dexterity makes since, but it should only be with very low dexterity
like if your DEX is 6 or 7 or lower.  BTW, I think fumbling abuses
dexterity, and if low dexterity causes fumbling then fumbling shouldn't
abuse dexterity cause it'll just keep getting lower and lower until you
find a unicorn horn or restore ability.
.  I found a glass pickaxe.  are those supposed to exist?  I put it away
in a little room in minetown assuming that it wouldn't work (I already
had a real pickaxe anyway), but would it work?  (If so, it shouldn't). I
should've tried it out.  I will if I find one again.

   I like being able to be a lawful elf, and an elf knight, but I made a
mistake with my elf knight. I was going to buy a round or two of
protection from the minetown priest but my warhorse killed the priest. I
not used to playing knights (or having pets which are tougher than a
large cat or dog).
  I also had very rusty speed boots because I'm not used to having pools
of water in the mines.  Obviously I should've been able to not walk into
the pools, but I'm also not used to not playing without tiles and it's
not as easy to notice the water there without tiles. (That's my excuse,
I know it's not a very good one, but it only happened twice and probably
not anymore.)

looking forward to future releases (and some fixed bugs)


